CsvLayoutSection = Warehouse layout (levels and allowed values)
CsvLayoutSub = The levels of each warehouse's hierarchy (e.g. Aisle › Shelf › Bin) and the values each level accepts. One file covers every warehouse.
CsvAssignSection = Bin assignments (product → bin)
CsvAssignSub = Which bin each product (and lot) sits in. One file per warehouse.
CsvStepExport = Export
CsvStepImport = Edit and import
CsvLayoutExportHint = Download every warehouse's layout, to edit or to use as a template.
CsvAssignExportHint = Pick a warehouse and download its assignments, with one column per level.
CsvImportHint = Save your edited sheet as CSV and upload it. You get a preview of every change; nothing is written until you confirm.
CsvFile = CSV file
CsvFormatAndRules = File format and import rules
CsvColumn = Column
CsvColumnMeaning = What it holds
CsvRules = On import
CsvColLayoutWarehouse = Warehouse ref, as on the warehouse card.
CsvColLayoutLevel = Position in the hierarchy: 1 is the top (e.g. Aisle), then 2, 3… Blank keeps the order of the rows.
CsvColLayoutLabel = Level name, e.g. Aisle or Shelf. Existing levels are matched on it.
CsvColLayoutType = text, number, list (dropdown) or letter (A, B, C…).
CsvColLayoutValues = For list and letter levels: the allowed values separated by a pipe, e.g. A|B|C. For letter, a single end code (Z, or AC to go past Z) generates the whole A…end range.
CsvRuleLayoutMatch = Levels are matched by label. A label not found in that warehouse creates a new level.
CsvRuleLayoutNoDelete = Missing allowed values are added. Nothing is deleted: levels and values left out of the file are kept, after the ones in it.
CsvRuleLayoutRight = Importing layouts needs the Binloc admin permission.
