#
# Hover help (tooltips on the "?" pictos and buttons)
#
LabelHelpWarehouse = Labels are per warehouse: each warehouse has its own levels, values and label layouts.
LabelHelpPrintFor = The level the labels are stuck on. A label is identified by the path from the top level down to this one (its full code); everything assigned below it is its contents, grouped by the next level down. Pick Shelf for shelf tags, Bag for bag tags.
LabelHelpProduct = Only bins holding products whose ref or label matches. While a product search is active, empty bins are not enumerated.
LabelHelpLevelFilter = Only bins under this %s value. With "Include empty bins", fixing a value here is also what lets a free-text level be enumerated.
LabelHelpRefresh = Apply the selection
LabelHelpReset = Clear the search and filters
PrintLabelsHint = Opens a print-only page and the print dialog. Sheet output: choose your paper. Label-printer output: choose the matching label stock and print at full scale, not fit-to-page.
BinValueLegendHint = What each dropdown or letter code means, from the value descriptions on the Warehouse Levels page. Shown on screen only — never printed.
LabelWidthHint = Label width as you read it. On a roll printer the shorter of width and height crosses the print head (Dymo LabelWriter: 56 mm max); orientation is handled by the printer driver.
LabelPadHint = Space between the label edge and its content.
LabelFontBodyHint = Base size for the contents; the title is 1.7 times this.
LabelSheetMarginHint = Blank margin around the whole grid on a sheet. Ignored for label-printer output.
LabelShowDescriptionHint = Prints the description of the label's own value under the title (e.g. "Left Rack" under "AL").
LabelShowProductLabelHint = Product name next to the ref on each item.
LabelShowBatchHint = Lot/serial number after each item that has one.
LabelLayoutSaveForLevelHint = Stores these settings for this level only; other levels keep the warehouse default.
LabelLayoutSaveAsDefaultHint = Stores these settings as the warehouse default, used by every level without its own layout.
LabelLayoutResetHint = Removes this level's own layout so the warehouse default applies again.
LevelTypeHelp = Text: free entry. Number: numeric entry. Dropdown: pick from a list of values you manage below. Letter: like Dropdown, but the values are letter codes (A–Z, then AA–ZZ) generated in one step instead of typed.
LevelLabelHelp = Shown on inputs, filters and labels, and used as the column header in CSV files. Renaming a level never touches stored data.
OptionValueHint = Short code that builds the bin name (e.g. L). Renaming it updates every assignment that uses it.
OptionDisableHint = Hides the value from new entry; existing assignments keep showing it, marked (legacy). Pending edits on the page are saved first.
OptionEnableHint = Makes the value available for new entry again. Pending edits on the page are saved first.
OptionDeleteHint = Removes the value. Only offered while nothing uses it. Pending edits on the page are saved first.
AddValueHint = Adds another empty row here; nothing is written until Save.
LevelsSaveHint = Saves everything on this page at once: level rows, every value and description, and all new values.
AddLevelHint = Adds a level row. Save to create it; a Dropdown or Letter level then shows its values editor below.
CopyLevelsHint = Copies another warehouse's levels and values into this one. Only offered while this warehouse has no levels.
GenerateLettersHint = Creates every missing code from A up to the one you enter: Z gives A–Z, AC continues past Z into AA, AB, AC. Existing values are kept. Pending edits on the page are saved first.
QuickAssignHint = Any product, with or without stock here: pick it, set its bin, Assign. It then appears in the table below.
BulkSaveAllHint = Saves every row that has a value. Blank inputs never erase stored values; rows marked with the trash icon are cleared.
SetSelectedToHint = Fills the ticked rows with the values you enter here (only the fields you fill). Nothing is written until Save All.
ConfirmSaveLayoutAsDefault = Save these settings as the warehouse default? Every level in this warehouse without a layout of its own will use them from now on.
ConfirmResetLayout = Remove the %s layout and fall back to the warehouse default? The settings stored for %s will be lost.

#
# Warehouse bin code prefix (entrepot extrafield binloc_code)
#
BinCodePrefix = Bin code prefix
BinCodePrefixHelp = One or two letters put in front of every bin code of this warehouse on labels (A + L21A4 = AL21A4), so identical layouts in different warehouses never share a code. Keep it unique across warehouses.
LabelShowWarehouse = Warehouse prefix (%s)
LabelWarehouseCodeUnset = not set
LabelShowWarehouseHint = Bakes the warehouse's Bin code prefix into every code on the label, so a bin in sea can A reads AL21A4 and the same bin in sea can B reads BL21A4. The prefix is set on the warehouse card (Bin code prefix field, listed under Stock extrafields).
LabelWarehouseCodeMissing = This warehouse has no %s yet, so codes print without one. Set it on the warehouse card.
LabelWarehouseCodeDuplicate = Bin code prefix "%s" is also used by warehouse %s — codes will not be unique across warehouses. Give each warehouse its own prefix.

#
# Pick / place sheets (PDF document models)
#
PickSheet = Pick sheet
PlaceSheet = Place sheet
BinlocPickSheetOrderModelDesc = Binloc pick sheet: bins to pick the unshipped quantity from, in walk order. Saved as REF-picksheet.pdf; never replaces the order PDF.
BinlocPickSheetShipmentModelDesc = Binloc pick sheet: bins of the exact warehouses and lots on this shipment, in walk order. Saved as REF-picksheet.pdf; never replaces the shipment PDF.
BinlocPlaceSheetModelDesc = Binloc place sheet: where each received line goes, with a write-in box for lines without a bin. Saved as REF-placesheet.pdf; never replaces the reception PDF.
SheetsSection = Pick / place sheets
SheetsSectionDesc = Adds a Binloc sheet to the document generator of the chosen objects (Documents block on the card). Enable the launch point that matches how your team picks — or both.
SheetForOrders = Pick sheet on sales orders
SheetForOrdersDesc = Pick before a shipment exists: lists the bins holding stock for the unshipped quantity, in the pick priority order set below (from the order's warehouse when set).
SheetForShipments = Pick sheet on shipments
SheetForShipmentsDesc = Pick after the shipment has chosen warehouses and lots: lists exactly those. Print it before validating if stock is decremented on validation.
SheetForReceptions = Place sheet on receptions
SheetForReceptionsDesc = Put-away list for received goods: assigned bin, suggested bin, or a write-in box.
SheetForMos = Pick sheet on manufacturing orders
SheetForMosDesc = Materials still to consume, from each line's warehouse (else the MO's, else any) in the pick priority order set below; then where the finished goods still to produce go.
BinlocPickSheetMoModelDesc = Binloc pick sheet: bins to pick the MO's remaining materials from, then where the finished goods go. Saved as REF-picksheet.pdf; never replaces the MO PDF.
SheetSectionMaterials = Materials to pick
SheetSectionOutput = Finished goods to put away
SheetNativeSetupLink = Module setup
SheetSplitByWarehouse = One section per warehouse
SheetSplitByWarehouseDesc = On: each warehouse starts on its own page (sites far apart). Off: one list in walking order across warehouses, grouped by bin code prefix.
PickPrioritySection = Pick priority
PickPrioritySectionDesc = Where sales order and manufacturing order sheets take stock from when a product is in several warehouses or lots. Shipment sheets list the warehouses and lots the shipment already names. Closed warehouses are never picked from.
PickPriority = Take stock from
PickPriorityBins = Locations with a bin first
PickPriorityBinsDesc = Stock whose exact product or lot has a bin first, then stock in a warehouse where the product has some bin, then stock with no bin. Keeps pickers on labelled shelves.
PickPriorityWarehouse = Warehouse order
PickPriorityWarehouseDesc = Warehouses in the order ranked below (lowest number first, unranked last), then locations with a bin first within a warehouse. Rank the closest or main store first to cut walking.
PickPriorityFewest = Fewest stops
PickPriorityFewestDesc = A location holding the whole quantity first, then locations with a bin, then the most stock, so a line is split across as few places as possible.
PickPrioritySmallest = Clear small stock first
PickPrioritySmallestDesc = Smallest quantities first, then locations with a bin, to empty nearly-empty spots and free space. Means more stops per line.
PickPriorityAlpha = Alphabetical (legacy)
PickPriorityAlphaDesc = Warehouses by reference, ignoring bins — the behaviour before 2.18.0.
PickPriorityOverExpiry = Pick priority beats lot expiry
PickPriorityOverExpiryDesc = Off: lot/serial products always take the earliest eat-by lot first, and the setting above only breaks ties. On: the setting above decides first and eat-by breaks ties.
PickWarehousePreferred = Document warehouse is a preference
PickWarehousePreferredDesc = Off: when the order, MO line or MO names a warehouse, only that warehouse is searched and a shortfall is reported there. On: it is searched first and the other warehouses, in pick priority order, cover the rest.
PickWarehouseOrder = Warehouse pick order
PickWarehouseOrderDesc = Lowest number is picked from first; leave blank for unranked (after ranked ones, by reference). Used by the Warehouse order setting, and in every other setting to break ties.
PickWarehouseRank = Rank
PickWarehouseClosed = Closed — never picked from
